# FaceFusion Python edits

Match upstream FaceFusion style: existing naming, types, and module layout.

## Preserve fork hooks

When editing files also changed upstream, keep fork-specific behavior:

| File | Fork behavior |
|------|---------------|
| `workflows/chunk_runner.py` | Entire file is fork-only — do not delete |
| `workflows/image_to_video.py` | Per-frame skip/retry + chunk env-var gating |
| `workflows/image_to_image.py` | Processor try/except graceful failure |
| `core.py` | `chunk-run` routing, `job_id` propagation |
| `program.py` | `chunk-run` subcommand registration |
| `exit_helper.py` | Diagnostic probes |
| `content_analyser.py` | NSFW gate disabled |

## Do not

- Silently revert fork patches while syncing upstream
- Add enhancer processors without explicit user request (Fix E baseline is enhancer-off)
- Change `chunk_size_frames` default without documenting in `WORKLOG.md`

## Tests

Fork test: `tests/test_chunk_runner.py`. Run via conda Python after workflow changes.
